Intellect bundles work from other MIT-licensed projects.

## sanidhyy/duolingo-clone ("Lingo")

Copyright (c) 2024 Sanidhya Kumar Verma — MIT License
https://github.com/sanidhyy/duolingo-clone

The learning interface in `ui/` is derived from that project: the button and
progress primitives, the lesson card / challenge / footer / header /
question-bubble / result-card components, and the snaking lesson-path button
geometry. The vendor stack around them (Next.js, Clerk, Stripe, Neon, Drizzle,
react-admin) was removed; the components now talk to this project's Python and
SQLite mastery engine instead.

Bundled assets under `ui/public/assets/` also come from that repository, which
in turn credits:

- Kenney Assets — https://kenney.nl/
- Freesound — https://freesound.org/
- ElevenLabs — https://elevenlabs.io/

Full upstream license text: https://github.com/sanidhyy/duolingo-clone/blob/main/LICENSE

## open-spaced-repetition/py-fsrs

Copyright (c) 2022 Open Spaced Repetition — MIT License
https://github.com/open-spaced-repetition/py-fsrs

`vendor/fsrs/` is the core of that project at commit 9446cb0: the Scheduler,
Card, Rating, ReviewLog, and State modules. The `torch`-dependent parameter
optimizer was deliberately excluded so this app keeps a standard-library-only
dependency story. It replaces a hand-rolled interval multiplier and now owns
when each question comes due; exam pressure still owns what is served first.
See DECISIONS/2026-09-20-search-open-source-first.md.
